WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:22.679
Wednesday afternoon Monster Academy students and teachers gathered in the lobby near the school's main entrance.

2
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.564
A white sheet covered a huge object that sat in the middle of the floor.

3
00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.937
"We'll finally get to see Mr.

4
00:00:30.977 --> 00:00:33.259
Freaky's sculpture," Winnie said to Ben.

5
00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:36.342
"Yep." Ben held up his notebook.

6
00:00:36.362 --> 00:00:39.224
"I'll be writing about it for my newspaper article."

7
00:00:40.065 --> 00:00:44.509
He looked around for Pixel, who was weaving in and out of the crowd with his camera.

8
00:00:44.529 --> 00:00:50.153
"And Pixel will take some great photos of it."

9
00:00:50.173 --> 00:00:52.095
"Lots of them!"

10
00:00:52.575 --> 00:00:53.596
the ghost chimed in.

11
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:57.339
Ms. Van Ghoul stood close to the sculpture with Mr.

12
00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:01.049
Freaky. She clapped her hands to get everyone's attention.

13
00:01:01.069 --> 00:01:02.630
"Listen up, students!"

14
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.611
"And please remain calm, everyone!"

15
00:01:06.011 --> 00:01:07.232
Mr. Freaky called out.

16
00:01:07.252 --> 00:01:10.373
"I know it's hard on such an exciting day!"

17
00:01:10.393 --> 00:01:12.054
Zzz. Zzz.

18
00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:17.276
At the back of the crowd, some zombies were snoring.

19
00:01:17.296 --> 00:01:20.637
"Well, I won't keep you waiting for one more minute."

20
00:01:21.318 --> 00:01:24.239
Mr. Freaky reached for the sheet covering his sculpture.

21
00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:26.700
With a quick yank, he pulled it away.

22
00:01:28.108 --> 00:01:31.150
Ben's eyes went wide, and his jaw dropped.

23
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:38.154
a piece of junk!"

24
00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:39.474
Mog burst out.

25
00:01:40.315 --> 00:01:41.075
Ben blinked.

26
00:01:41.735 --> 00:01:46.038
Mog was right—the whole thing was made from junk and metal scraps.

27
00:01:46.858 --> 00:01:54.382
Car bumpers and hoods, along with fan blades, antennas, tools, and other metal objects had been welded together

28
00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:57.244
to form one gigantic junk sculpture.

29
00:01:58.548 --> 00:02:01.589
The artwork rested on six mismatched wheels.

30
00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.010
A blob moved closer for a better look.

31
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.591
"Um, Mr.

32
00:02:07.651 --> 00:02:09.931
Freaky What is that thing?"

33
00:02:11.292 --> 00:02:15.393
Mr. Freaky puffed out his chest as Pixel started taking photos.

34
00:02:15.413 --> 00:02:19.714
"I call it Moving Inspiration!"

35
00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.655
"Moving?" somebody said.

36
00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.615
"It's just sitting there.

37
00:02:25.035 --> 00:02:26.636
It looks like a junkyard to me."

38
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.721
"Oh!" Mr.

39
00:02:29.761 --> 00:02:31.261
Freaky slapped his forehead.

40
00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:33.122
"I forgot to plug it in!"

41
00:02:37.644 --> 00:02:39.905
He plugged a long cord into the wall.

42
00:02:42.286 --> 00:02:46.787
With a cough and a sputter, the massive sculpture began to whirl in place.

43
00:02:49.348 --> 00:02:50.309
Ben snickered.

44
00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:55.791
"Now it looks like a junkyard on wheels," he whispered to Winnie.

45
00:02:56.511 --> 00:02:57.952
Ms. Van Ghoul was beaming.

46
00:02:58.632 --> 00:03:01.933
"Remember, students—art is in the eye of the beholder.

47
00:03:03.053 --> 00:03:05.234
That's the magic of art and Art Week.

48
00:03:05.594 --> 00:03:08.895
We learn to appreciate new forms of beauty!"

49
00:03:08.915 --> 00:03:12.456
"I wouldn't exactly call that thing beautiful."

50
00:03:13.076 --> 00:03:14.236
Ben scratched his head.

51
00:03:14.256 --> 00:03:17.277
"How on earth will I describe it in my story?"

52
00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:21.458
"That's going to be a challenge," Winnie said.

53
00:03:21.478 --> 00:03:22.699
"I'm sure Mr.

54
00:03:22.759 --> 00:03:27.720
Freaky is expecting very positive reviews of Moving Junkyard.

55
00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.150
I mean, Moving Inspiration."

56
00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.992
They both laughed.

57
00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:37.375
Then Winnie glanced at a clock on the wall.

58
00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:40.537
"I've got to get back to the gym.

59
00:03:40.998 --> 00:03:42.199
We started painting today."

60
00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:43.880
"How's it going?"

61
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:44.901
Ben asked.

62
00:03:44.921 --> 00:03:46.582
"Are you guys making progress?"

63
00:03:47.943 --> 00:03:49.905
"Slow progress," Winnie said.

64
00:03:49.925 --> 00:03:53.528
"We still have a lot to do before Friday, but I think it'll be okay."

65
00:03:53.548 --> 00:03:56.710
"It'll be more than okay," Ben said.

66
00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:03.174
"Your flying painting will be the big hit of Art Week—bigger even than da Creepy's new painting."

67
00:04:03.194 --> 00:04:06.155
"I don't know about that," Winnie said.

68
00:04:06.175 --> 00:04:08.056
"But thanks for the vote of confidence."

69
00:04:09.656 --> 00:04:13.998
With that, she hurried off, and Ben went over to interview a skeleton.

70
00:04:14.018 --> 00:04:15.459
"Do you have a minute?

71
00:04:15.859 --> 00:04:17.540
I'd like to get your opinion about Mr.

72
00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.540
Freaky's sculpture."

73
00:04:21.881 --> 00:04:23.902
The skeleton spoke in a low voice.

74
00:04:23.922 --> 00:04:25.903
"Is this on the record?"

75
00:04:25.923 --> 00:04:28.924
"Actually, it is," Ben replied.

76
00:04:28.944 --> 00:04:31.246
"It's for my article for the school paper."

77
00:04:31.266 --> 00:04:34.868
"Sorry! I'm super busy right now!"

78
00:04:35.948 --> 00:04:38.270
The skeleton clattered off down the hallway.

79
00:04:40.311 --> 00:04:45.574
With a sigh, Ben spun around and scanned the monsters who were still hanging around the lobby.

80
00:04:46.254 --> 00:04:51.677
Who would say something positive about— "Mog!"

81
00:04:52.077 --> 00:04:53.638
Ben hurried over to his friend.

82
00:04:53.658 --> 00:04:56.980
"What do you think of Moving Inspiration?"

83
00:04:57.776 --> 00:05:00.418
Mog glanced at the sculpture and rubbed his chin.

84
00:05:00.438 --> 00:05:03.661
"It's okay, I guess.

85
00:05:04.142 --> 00:05:05.903
I mean, at first I didn't get it.

86
00:05:06.504 --> 00:05:08.325
I didn't know you could make art out of junk."

87
00:05:09.266 --> 00:05:10.727
Ben jotted down some notes.

88
00:05:11.828 --> 00:05:16.792
"So it sounds like you find Moving Inspiration inspiring?"

89
00:05:18.093 --> 00:05:18.874
Mog nodded.

90
00:05:18.894 --> 00:05:20.675
"Yeah, I think I do."

91
00:05:20.695 --> 00:05:22.817
"Psst! Mog!"

92
00:05:23.217 --> 00:05:23.978
a voice said.

93
00:05:24.519 --> 00:05:25.780
Ben and Mog looked over.

94
00:05:26.804 --> 00:05:30.427
The Doppel Gang stood nearby, waving for Mog to join them.

95
00:05:30.447 --> 00:05:34.049
"Want to walk around school and check out some more art?"

96
00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:35.130
Carly said.

97
00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.712
"Sure," Mog said.

98
00:05:39.213 --> 00:05:40.694
Ms. Van Ghoul smiled.

99
00:05:40.714 --> 00:05:44.156
"Why don't you monsters go to the art room?"

100
00:05:44.596 --> 00:05:45.077
she said.

101
00:05:45.097 --> 00:05:49.540
"The mummies are building pyramids out of straws.

102
00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.801
I'm sure they could use some help."

103
00:05:54.483 --> 00:05:57.526
"That sounds fun," Larry said, winking at Mog.

104
00:05:57.546 --> 00:05:58.908
"Come on!"

105
00:06:06.257 --> 00:06:10.822
careful, Mog," Ben said under his breath as he watched them go.
